      "timestamp": "2026-09-25T11:58:59.025878Z",
      "user_text": "Expand a field operator in a **spin-dependent basis**: $\\hat\\psi_\\sigma(\\mathbf x)=\\sum_m \\varphi_{m\\sigma}(\\mathbf x)\\hat c_{m\\sigma}$. The coefficients are then all-space integrals BY DEFINITION. The basis is arbitrary, so there is nothing to carry out — the integral IS the definition. What the notebook has to offer is not \"it computes\" but \"it can be written down and used afterwards\".",
      "visible_action": "Memo",
      "operation": null,
      "operation_args": {},
      "backend": null,
      "rendered_command": null,
      "show_command_to_user": false,
      "input_refs": [],
